  "content": [
    {
      "text": "in thee shall all families of the earth be blessed, Gen. 12:3 (Gal. 3:8; Abr. 2:11–16). all the nations of the earth shall be blessed in him, Gen. 18:18 (22:18; 26:4; 28:14; Acts 3:25; 1 Ne. 15:18). unto him shall the gathering of the people be, Gen. 49:10. I will take you to me for a people, Ex. 6:7 (Lev. 26:12; Ezek. 11:20; 14:11). a kingdom of priests, and an holy nation, Ex. 19:6 (1 Pet. 2:9). Lord … hath chosen thee to be a special people, Deut. 7:6. Lord hath avouched thee … to be his peculiar people, Deut. 26:18 (1 Pet. 2:9). all people of the earth may know thy name, 1 Kgs. 8:43. all nations shall flow unto it, Isa. 2:2. root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign … to it shall the Gentiles seek, Isa. 11:10 (2 Ne. 21:10). strangers shall … cleave to the house of Jacob, Isa. 14:1 (2 Ne. 24:1). In that day shall Israel be … a blessing, Isa. 19:24. Thou art my servant; I have chosen thee, Isa. 41:9. Ye are my witnesses … and my servant, Isa. 43:10. give thee for a light to the Gentiles, Isa. 49:6. say to the prisoners, Go forth, Isa. 49:9. nations that knew not thee shall run unto thee, Isa. 55:5. will I gather others to him, beside those that are gathered, Isa. 56:8. Gentiles shall come to thy light, Isa. 60:3. they might be called trees of righteousness, Isa. 61:3. they shall declare my glory among the Gentiles, Isa. 66:19. In the day when I chose Israel, Ezek. 20:5.",
